## Context

Ticket 0879 rerouted the REROLL bump out of the isolated verify-gate: the gate
writes nothing and the bump line travels in the verdict's `reroll_bump:` field,
posed by the orchestrator with verb `note` (PR #1164). Three consumers of the
bump line were outside that PR's edit scope and still describe the old recipe.

Found by the #1164 review panel (correctness, consistency, red team, doc
propagation seats, round 1).

## Scope

- `skills/raid/SKILL.md` wrap-up tally (~L368-372): `grep -h ' bump '
  tickets/*.erg | awk '{print $4}'` matches the old verb; new REROLL bumps read
  `note verify-reroll — round {n}: …`, so the "Y verify-reroll" count silently
  drops to zero, and `$4` names the wrong field even on a match. Match
  `note verify-reroll` and count on the right field.
- `skills/raid/SKILL.md` circuit-breaker recipe (~L382-384): hand-writes
  `{ISO8601} claude bump circuit-breaker — {reason}` into the main-repo
  tickets/. That is a hand-written append with the verb `bump` -- the exact
  shape ticket 0879 was filed over. Route it through `erg log <id> "note
  circuit-breaker — {reason}"`, which now lands the line well-formed.
- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` fork-liveness fallback (~L124, L138): "log a bump
  line on the ticket" reads as permission to run `erg log` on main mid-wave;
  it should point at the reroll_bump posing rule (orchestrator poses onto the
  PR branch or defers to merge time).

- A manual `/verify-gate` run outside the raid/gaze flow (round-2 panel
  note): the verdict comment keeps a durable copy, but nothing names the
  caller who poses the line onto the PR branch. State it in
  `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` (the caller of a bare gate run poses the
  reroll_bump line, or defers to the merge).

## Exit criteria

- [x] The wrap-up tally counts `note verify-reroll` bumps
- [x] The circuit-breaker recipe goes through erg log with verb note
- [x] The gaze fork-liveness fallback names the reroll_bump posing rule
- [x] make check passes

